      "obligation": "refuter:61:1",
      "id": "thm-interval-hermitian-ldl-inertia-certifier-soundness",
      "location": "Proof, step 1.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The algorithm’s Definition says, “For a successful candidate plan, independently initialize the interval active matrix from the family enclosure and process the same blocks.” It does not explicitly apply the input permutation to that enclosure. Yet this proof step asserts, “Initially the active interval matrix encloses each permuted family member.” The outward-update dependency only propagates an enclosure; it does not establish that the initial matrix is the permuted enclosure. Specify applying the permutation to the interval enclosure, or adjust the proof to the initialization actually defined.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
      "observed_sha256": "c0ef0e1bda1bc7398e5935d2818074890dd9d13bc99b2cee5e1dca05178afff1"
    }
  ],
